---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy | Block and Site"
  description="What information Block and Site collects through this website, how it is stored in HubSpot, and how to ask us to delete it. We never sell your information."
>
  <Header />
  <main id="main" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="prose">
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p class="effective">Effective date: [EFFECTIVE DATE]</p>

        <p>
          This policy explains what information {site.name} collects through this website and what we do with it. The
          short version: we only collect what you give us in our contact form, plus basic information about which pages
          you visit. We store it in HubSpot, use it to reply to you, and never sell it.
        </p>

        <h2>Information you give us</h2>
        <p>When you fill out our contact form, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>First and last name</li>
          <li>Email address</li>
          <li>Phone number (if you provide it)</li>
          <li>Business name</li>
          <li>Current website address (if you provide it)</li>
          <li>Your message (if you write one)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We don’t ask for payment details, passwords, or any other sensitive information on this website.</p>

        <h2>Pages you visit (cookies)</h2>
        <p>
          This website uses HubSpot’s tracking code, which sets cookies in your browser. These cookies let us see which
          pages of our site you viewed and, if you fill out the contact form, connect those page views to your
          submission. HubSpot may also record technical details such as your browser type, device, and approximate
          location based on your IP address.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings. The site will still work, and you can still contact
          us.
        </p>

        <h2>How we use your information</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To reply to your request and send you a website review</li>
          <li>To follow up about our services if you’ve asked us to work with you</li>
          <li>To understand which pages on our site are useful</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where it’s stored</h2>
        <p>
          Contact form submissions and page-view information are stored in HubSpot, the customer relationship management
          (CRM) service we use. HubSpot processes this information on our behalf. You can read
          <a href="https://legal.hubspot.com/privacy-policy" rel="noopener">HubSpot’s privacy policy</a>. Our website is hosted
          on Cloudflare, which processes basic request information to deliver the site.
        </p>

        <h2>We never sell your information</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We only share it with the service providers listed
          above, which we use to run this website and our business, or if the law requires it.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>[RETENTION PERIOD: how long you keep contact records before deleting them]</p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us to show you, correct, or delete the information we have about you, or to stop contacting you.
          Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we’ll take care of it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>If we change this policy, we’ll update it on this page and change the effective date above.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          {site.name}<br />
          {site.mailingAddress.street}, {site.mailingAddress.city}, {site.mailingAddress.region} {site.mailingAddress.postalCode}<br />
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .effective { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: var(--s2); }
  h1 { font-size: var(--step-3); }
</style>
